---
description: |
  Reads a stream of Cisco Secure Firewall ASA syslog and parses each message.

  Accepts newline-delimited and octet-counted messages with and without
  priority, timestamp, and device ID, in the EMBLEM and RFC 5424 formats, and
  behind the header of a syslog relay.
args:
  named:
    - name: timezone
      type: string
      default: null
      description: |
        The time zone of times without a zone, as an IANA name such as
        `Europe/Berlin` or as a UTC offset such as `+01:00`. Defaults to UTC.
    - name: reference
      type: time
      default: null
      description: |
        The time that timestamps without a year precede. Defaults to now. Set it
        to the end of logs that are older than about a year.
---

read_syslog accept_pri_only=true, raw_message=raw_message
// Lines without priority and timestamp continue the previous message, or have
// no raw message when there is none. An ASA message never spans lines.
select line=(raw_message? else syslog_message).split("\n")
unroll line
cisco::asa::parse message=line, timezone=$timezone, reference=$reference
